From 6cf7a734ba8d821fba26e89901b9815d4b6b6d07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 07:08:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10086/11362] [outer-loop] Unattended cross-run supervisor
 refinement (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6720)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6640 made redirects measurable, but each run's receipt died
with its scratch directory, and nothing turned outcomes into a durable
record. This ships the between-runs step for CLAUDE.md generalization-floor
activity 4: `scripts/arc_supervisor_refine.py` ingests APPLIED
trajectory-supervisor receipts from rows.json files into a deduplicated
ledger at `ops/arc_supervisor_refinement_ledger.json`, then applies a
frozen evidence contract that only RECOMMENDS. A human applies changes.

Contract, with the why in the spec: floor of 10 firings per arm
(0.75^10 = 0.056 — the smallest all-zero count that rejects a 25% follow
rate near the 5% level; the sibling Exp6524 floor of 2 lets a coin flip
pass), Wilson 90% bounds, three rules: retire (10 fired, 0 helped), raise
priority (interval separation vs the pooled other arms — comparative
because the post-hoc metric credits every pending redirect on one
level-up, observed live at action 353), and a written new-arm
specification for a human when every arm fired and stagnation continued.
Shadow receipts and error markers are counted, never ingested. Directory
scans prune any directory holding a .git entry (the 2026-08-25 nested
repo-clone corpus-inflation trap).

Against the current live data (9 receipts, 6 redirects, each arm at
2 fired / 1 helped) the tool reports INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE, loudly, and
that is the honest answer. A no-firings ledger reports
no_firings_nothing_to_refine, which satisfies the floor slot.

Verification: spec section REQ-ARC-WMTE-6720 + SCENARIO-1..7 (landed via
the conductor checkpoint commit 0e961586cf that swept the in-progress
append); 15 tests pass with --no-cov; 8 mutations (filter, dedupe, floor,
retire, promote comparison, new-arm boundary, no-firings status, clone
pruning) each RED in a PYTHONPATH-pinned worktree with the interpreter's
import file verified, then restored to GREEN. Ruff and focused mypy clean.

Considered and rejected: wiring the step into the harness's main() (a live
GPU run was in flight; the CLI is invoked between runs instead), and
scipy-backed intervals (the unattended step must not grow a dependency).

